WEBVTT

00:00:08.500 --> 00:00:09.333
Let's see...

00:00:09.333 --> 00:00:14.375
"Experimental result: Human is dead. Mismatch."

00:00:14.375 --> 00:00:16.667
Human is dead?

00:00:16.667 --> 00:00:18.125
Yeah...

00:00:18.125 --> 00:00:19.583
Someone...

00:00:21.500 --> 00:00:23.083
...died?

00:00:23.083 --> 00:00:25.250
Yeah... I think so.

00:00:25.250 --> 00:00:26.125
What else does it say?!

00:00:26.125 --> 00:00:30.583
Umm... "The details are
in Jellyman's Report #14."

00:00:30.583 --> 00:00:33.042
Jellyman's Report? What's that?

00:00:33.042 --> 00:00:35.083
How would I know?

00:00:35.083 --> 00:00:38.917
But there's this strange
database on the server...

00:00:38.917 --> 00:00:40.500
What's this?!

00:00:40.500 --> 00:00:43.208
I think it's some kind of programming code.

00:00:52.583 --> 00:00:54.417
--Daru-<i>kun</i>?
--I have no idea!

00:00:54.417 --> 00:00:55.917
I can't make any sense of this!

00:00:55.917 --> 00:00:58.917
Die! Dammit!

00:00:58.917 --> 00:01:02.458
Maybe we should stop.

00:01:02.458 --> 00:01:06.333
I've finally experienced one of those,
"And I was so close too!" moments.

00:01:06.333 --> 00:01:08.875
Good work. You can rest now.

00:01:08.875 --> 00:01:11.167
Don't have to tell me that. I'm licked.

00:01:11.167 --> 00:01:13.167
I got some canned <i>oden</i>, Daru-<i>kun</i>!

00:01:13.167 --> 00:01:14.333
Thanks.

00:01:14.333 --> 00:01:16.208
Programming code...

00:01:16.208 --> 00:01:21.500
The IBN 5100 was built
before PCs could run BASIC,

00:01:21.500 --> 00:01:24.417
so it can read IBN's proprietary
programming language or something--

00:01:24.417 --> 00:01:29.750
The IBN 5100's abilities are
needed to halt SERN's plans.

00:01:29.750 --> 00:01:32.625
I'd very much like to talk with you sometime.

00:01:32.625 --> 00:01:34.917
This is my e-mail address.

00:01:34.917 --> 00:01:37.917
If you contact me, I'll reply.

00:01:54.583 --> 00:01:59.792
<i>suu juuoku mono kodou no kazu sae</i>

00:01:59.792 --> 00:02:06.458
<i>anata ni wa matataki teido no saji na toukyuu</i>

00:02:06.458 --> 00:02:11.667
<i>kako ni torawarete mirai o nageku mo</i>

00:02:11.667 --> 00:02:17.583
<i>chiri hitotsu gosan o yurusanu hitsuzen</i>

00:02:17.583 --> 00:02:23.708
<i>mugen ni hirogaru yume mo egaku mirai mo</i>

00:02:23.708 --> 00:02:29.542
<i>bokutachi ni yurusareta kyoei no kenri</i>

00:02:29.542 --> 00:02:35.792
<i>yuugen sore wa futatsu no hari ga shimesu</i>

00:02:35.792 --> 00:02:40.375
<i>zankoku na yakujou to sentaku e</i>

00:02:40.375 --> 00:02:42.625
<i>Hacking to the Gate</i>

00:02:42.625 --> 00:02:49.542
<i>da kara ima ichi byou</i>
<i>goto ni sekaisen o koete</i>

00:02:49.542 --> 00:02:54.458
<i>kimi no sono egao mamoritai no sa</i>

00:02:54.458 --> 00:03:01.458
<i>soshite mata kanashimi</i>
<i>no nai jikan no ruupu e to</i>

00:03:01.458 --> 00:03:08.125
<i>nomi komarete yuku kodoku no kansokusha</i>

00:03:13.375 --> 00:03:16.292
So much laundry!

00:03:17.833 --> 00:03:22.458
Yeah, with all these all-nighters,
Daru and I haven't been home yet.

00:03:22.458 --> 00:03:24.833
What's more, all of Daru's
clothes--from T-shirts to underwear--

00:03:24.833 --> 00:03:26.417
are size XXXL.

00:03:26.417 --> 00:03:31.208
--Oh! It's Faris-<i>chan</i>!
--Okabe Rintaro!

00:03:32.167 --> 00:03:34.292
Whassup!

00:03:35.167 --> 00:03:36.458
Let me warn you.

00:03:36.458 --> 00:03:40.000
First, my name is Hououin Kyouma.

00:03:40.000 --> 00:03:43.667
--Second, that greeting is dangerously--
--Whassup, Suzu-<i>san</i>!

00:03:43.667 --> 00:03:45.208
Not you too!

00:03:45.208 --> 00:03:47.167
Wait, since when do you know each other?

00:03:47.167 --> 00:03:50.792
We share the same building.
It's natural to at least be acquaintances.

00:03:50.792 --> 00:03:54.333
Suzu-<i>san </i>gave me this Rai-Net card!

00:03:54.333 --> 00:03:56.750
A gold one!

00:03:56.750 --> 00:03:58.083
Where are you going?

00:03:58.083 --> 00:03:59.417
To do laundry.

00:03:59.417 --> 00:04:02.458
Okarin and Daru-<i>kun </i>have
been up all night for days now.

00:04:02.458 --> 00:04:04.292
Part-timer!

00:04:04.292 --> 00:04:07.000
Take your work seriously or I'll fire you.

00:04:07.000 --> 00:04:09.042
Yikes...

00:04:09.042 --> 00:04:12.458
And keep your hands off my part-timer, Okabe.

00:04:12.458 --> 00:04:17.125
Are you sure <i>you're </i>not the
one lusting after her, Mr. Braun?

00:04:17.125 --> 00:04:22.958
Talk like that in front of
Nae and I'll seriously kill you.

00:04:22.958 --> 00:04:25.750
Nae? Oh, that little critter?

00:04:25.750 --> 00:04:28.583
Don't call my daughter an animal!

00:04:28.583 --> 00:04:32.042
Why would I lust after my
part-timer anyway?! She's just a kid!

00:04:32.042 --> 00:04:34.917
I'm not a kid! I'm a full-fledged warrior!

00:04:34.917 --> 00:04:35.792
Huh?

00:04:35.792 --> 00:04:37.750
That's a nice look, part-time warrior.

00:04:37.750 --> 00:04:39.458
Always remember it

00:04:39.458 --> 00:04:42.583
and someday you'll change
classes and become a true warrior--

00:04:42.583 --> 00:04:44.750
Be quiet. Every time you talk--

00:04:44.750 --> 00:04:47.167
Really, I <i>am </i>a warrior!

00:04:47.167 --> 00:04:52.167
Why do all the weirdos gather here?

00:04:53.333 --> 00:04:55.417
Later.

00:04:55.417 --> 00:04:56.833
We're also--

00:05:02.958 --> 00:05:06.417
That's one of Mayuri's habits.

00:05:06.417 --> 00:05:10.208
I've dubbed it the "Stardust Shake Hand."

00:05:15.708 --> 00:05:20.667
I wonder if I can reach the stars...

00:05:20.667 --> 00:05:22.958
You can't even see them.

00:05:22.958 --> 00:05:28.708
The stars are still there
during the day too, you know.

00:05:32.458 --> 00:05:35.000
Those <i>were </i>powerful EM waves.

00:05:35.000 --> 00:05:39.500
They definitely could've caused
a cell phone to malfunction.

00:05:39.500 --> 00:05:42.042
But that banana...

00:05:42.042 --> 00:05:46.542
This Phone Microwave
(Temporary Name) is a time machine!

00:05:46.542 --> 00:05:48.292
Yeah, right.

00:05:56.458 --> 00:05:58.417
Faris-<i>chan</i>...

00:05:58.417 --> 00:06:00.917
How did this happen to you?

00:06:00.917 --> 00:06:04.167
--I'm closing it.
--Okay...

00:06:04.167 --> 00:06:08.833
Daru is just like the
universe--continually expanding.

00:06:11.000 --> 00:06:13.125
Shining Finger, huh?

00:06:13.125 --> 00:06:17.250
What's taking Titor so long?
He told me to message him!

00:06:17.250 --> 00:06:19.708
"Tell me how to contact the Super hax0r..."

00:06:19.708 --> 00:06:21.250
Man, she's persistent!

00:06:24.667 --> 00:06:26.792
Thank you for contacting me.

00:06:26.792 --> 00:06:29.750
Regarding the image of the program you sent,

00:06:29.750 --> 00:06:33.958
it's indeed an IBN
proprietary programming language.

00:06:33.958 --> 00:06:38.125
To decode it, you will require an IBN 5100.

00:06:40.375 --> 00:06:41.458
Listen up!

00:06:41.458 --> 00:06:46.750
The Future Gadget Laboratory will
now initiate its top-secret emergency plan!

00:06:51.792 --> 00:06:54.958
What's going on, Okarin?

00:06:54.958 --> 00:06:57.458
Wake up, Daru!

00:06:57.458 --> 00:06:59.875
Our battle with the massive secret organization

00:06:59.875 --> 00:07:02.583
that rules the world from
the shadows begins now!

00:07:02.583 --> 00:07:04.708
Hnn? Whazzuh...?

00:07:04.708 --> 00:07:06.375
I'm talking about SERN!

00:07:07.500 --> 00:07:12.667
They're a worldwide
organization bent on evil research

00:07:12.667 --> 00:07:15.792
and the mastermind of a vast conspiracy!

00:07:15.792 --> 00:07:19.000
The world doesn't need <i>two </i>mad scientists!

00:07:19.000 --> 00:07:22.792
We must beat them to the
punch before they beat us!

00:07:22.792 --> 00:07:25.667
I don't understand a thing you're saying.

00:07:25.667 --> 00:07:29.042
First, we need to get
our hands on an IBN 5100!

00:07:29.042 --> 00:07:32.083
Then we decode SERN's mysterious program!

00:07:32.083 --> 00:07:37.292
--Prepare to depart!
--But Mayushii has work today...

00:07:40.167 --> 00:07:42.583
So it's all up to me now...

00:07:45.708 --> 00:07:48.750
Trading information might be an idea...

00:07:55.333 --> 00:07:57.208
Oh, Assistant.

00:07:57.208 --> 00:07:59.292
Not so fast.

00:07:59.292 --> 00:08:01.375
--What do you want?!
--Come with me.

00:08:01.375 --> 00:08:03.417
H-Hey!

00:08:04.417 --> 00:08:07.458
You messed up the shoulder part here...

00:08:07.458 --> 00:08:09.833
"Almost no info here."

00:08:09.833 --> 00:08:11.875
Useless louse!

00:08:11.875 --> 00:08:17.042
--So why are you glaring at <i>me</i>?
--Fear not. You aren't the cause.

00:08:17.042 --> 00:08:19.458
I'd appreciate you not taking
your frustration out on me.

00:08:19.458 --> 00:08:21.458
Sulking, are we?

00:08:21.458 --> 00:08:25.042
Mayuri was worried that you might be cross.

00:08:25.042 --> 00:08:28.917
You're too old to be
acting like a kid, you know.

00:08:28.917 --> 00:08:31.750
You're in absolutely no position to talk.

00:08:31.750 --> 00:08:33.958
Anyway, what did you want to talk about?

00:08:33.958 --> 00:08:35.583
It's simple.

00:08:35.583 --> 00:08:38.625
Quit sulking and come back
to the lab to work, Christina.

00:08:38.625 --> 00:08:41.333
You can at <i>least </i>stick to calling me one name.

00:08:41.333 --> 00:08:43.167
Listen when people are talking, The Zombie!

00:08:43.167 --> 00:08:45.375
<i>You're </i>the one not listening here!

00:08:46.375 --> 00:08:49.375
How did I ever get involved with this guy?

00:08:49.375 --> 00:08:53.542
I want to punch myself for
being so curious back then.

00:08:53.542 --> 00:08:55.000
Wha...? <i>Again</i>?!

00:08:55.000 --> 00:08:56.917
Are those messages that annoying?

00:08:56.917 --> 00:08:59.458
It's absolutely insane how--

00:08:59.458 --> 00:09:02.458
Wait, could she be an Organization agent too?!

00:09:02.458 --> 00:09:04.292
Organization? What's that?

00:09:04.292 --> 00:09:05.667
The Organization is the Organization!

00:09:05.667 --> 00:09:09.750
A secret, transnational organization that
controls the world from the shadows and--

00:09:09.750 --> 00:09:13.417
Sounds like an average
conspiracy theory. Thank you very--

00:09:13.417 --> 00:09:16.417
--What's wrong?
--N-Nothing.

00:09:19.333 --> 00:09:21.000
Really! It's nothing!

00:09:21.000 --> 00:09:23.833
Keep asking me and I'll slug you!

00:09:23.833 --> 00:09:25.917
Lashing out, huh? Come with me.

00:09:25.917 --> 00:09:29.542
I'll give you your mission...
after we retrieve the laundry.

00:09:29.542 --> 00:09:30.708
Huh?

00:09:30.708 --> 00:09:33.250
Do you honestly think I'll just blindly follow--

00:09:33.250 --> 00:09:35.583
Laundry?

00:09:35.583 --> 00:09:38.417
Oh, so this is where it is.

00:09:38.417 --> 00:09:40.417
You don't have one at the hotel?

00:09:40.417 --> 00:09:42.917
No, it's a pretty fancy hotel.

00:09:42.917 --> 00:09:48.500
But it's not my style to send
everything I wear out for cleaning.

00:09:48.500 --> 00:09:50.708
You found it, thanks to me.

00:09:50.708 --> 00:09:52.625
Be grateful and--

00:09:52.625 --> 00:09:54.917
--Still no change?
--Of course not.

00:09:54.917 --> 00:09:57.125
You don't think spinning will
cause something to happen, do you?

00:09:57.125 --> 00:10:02.250
The answer is often hidden
in what seems most obvious.

00:10:02.250 --> 00:10:05.000
Who would've imagined hooking
a phone up to a microwave...

00:10:05.000 --> 00:10:07.917
--...would produce a time machine--
--It's not a time machine!

00:10:07.917 --> 00:10:09.042
Huh?

00:10:09.042 --> 00:10:11.125
It's some kind of mistake!

00:10:11.125 --> 00:10:15.708
Time machines are nothing but pseudoscience.

00:10:15.708 --> 00:10:18.583
I refuse to have any part of it.

00:10:18.583 --> 00:10:22.000
Why do you insist on denying what you saw?

00:10:22.000 --> 00:10:23.958
I'm not.

00:10:23.958 --> 00:10:26.583
Could it be due to past trauma?!

00:10:26.583 --> 00:10:29.500
Yes, when she was five,

00:10:29.500 --> 00:10:32.667
Christina was struck by
lightning on the plains of Arkansas--

00:10:32.667 --> 00:10:33.875
No, I wasn't.

00:10:33.875 --> 00:10:35.375
Then why?

00:10:35.375 --> 00:10:39.125
I already explained why.
It's theoretically impossible.

00:10:39.125 --> 00:10:42.250
Theories are nothing more
than lexical entertainment.

00:10:42.250 --> 00:10:46.000
Just accept what you saw.

00:10:46.000 --> 00:10:48.292
No.

00:10:48.292 --> 00:10:50.958
--Why are you so stubborn to--
--I said no!

00:10:50.958 --> 00:10:53.292
I won't...

00:10:53.292 --> 00:10:56.125
I won't repeat my father's failure!

00:10:57.750 --> 00:11:00.667
I'm sorry. I got emotional.

00:11:06.292 --> 00:11:07.458
Don't worry about it!

00:11:07.458 --> 00:11:12.167
I purposely angered you
to ascertain how you think--

00:11:15.458 --> 00:11:19.333
Anyway, the Phone
Microwave is <i>not </i>a time machine.

00:11:19.333 --> 00:11:21.042
Understood.

00:11:21.042 --> 00:11:24.042
I apologize for forcing you to join our lab.

00:11:24.042 --> 00:11:26.208
You needn't come anymore.

00:11:26.208 --> 00:11:28.542
But I <i>will </i>tell you this...

00:11:28.542 --> 00:11:32.583
The title of Lab Member 004
will be set aside forever.

00:11:32.583 --> 00:11:35.792
That number will always be yours.

00:11:35.792 --> 00:11:38.500
Quit trying to act cool!

00:11:38.500 --> 00:11:41.208
What's the big idea?!
That was the perfect farewell speech!

00:11:41.208 --> 00:11:42.708
And it annoys me!

00:11:42.708 --> 00:11:46.208
You still have laundry here. <i>I'll </i>leave.

00:11:46.208 --> 00:11:48.125
Bye.

00:11:48.125 --> 00:11:50.542
--What?!
--That's payback.

00:11:50.542 --> 00:11:55.333
I suggest you reflect on the error of your ways.

00:11:55.333 --> 00:11:57.125
Yeah, fine. Bye.

00:11:57.125 --> 00:11:58.250
Wait.

00:11:58.250 --> 00:11:59.542
Quit grabbing me there!

00:11:59.542 --> 00:12:03.375
Do you know anything about the IBN 5100?

00:12:03.375 --> 00:12:04.792
IBN?

00:12:04.792 --> 00:12:06.792
An old PC.

00:12:06.792 --> 00:12:10.042
--What are you going to use it for?
--Curious to know?

00:12:13.292 --> 00:12:14.792
You are, aren't you?

00:12:14.792 --> 00:12:16.417
Urgh...

00:12:16.417 --> 00:12:19.625
Just a little.

00:12:19.625 --> 00:12:23.542
The IBN 5100 is connected to SERN's secrets.

00:12:23.542 --> 00:12:24.708
Huh?

00:12:24.708 --> 00:12:28.542
SERN is researching time travel,

00:12:28.542 --> 00:12:35.083
and we need the IBN 5100's unique
functionality to decode their secret program.

00:12:35.083 --> 00:12:38.583
Well? Are you shocked?

00:12:38.583 --> 00:12:40.542
Ridiculous. What a waste of time.

00:12:40.542 --> 00:12:43.083
Y-You scoffed at me!

00:12:43.083 --> 00:12:44.583
Curse you!

00:12:44.583 --> 00:12:47.333
Well, I'll show you!

00:12:47.333 --> 00:12:51.375
Just you wait, Christina!

00:12:51.375 --> 00:12:53.542
I told you not to call me that...

00:12:53.542 --> 00:12:59.167
--SERN is researching time travel...
--We need the IBN 5100's unique functionality...

00:12:59.167 --> 00:13:02.042
What nerve. I only told her
'cause she said she was curious...

00:13:03.083 --> 00:13:04.083
A PC?

00:13:04.083 --> 00:13:06.125
Yeah, an old one.

00:13:06.125 --> 00:13:09.292
I think it costs 5100 yen or something...

00:13:09.292 --> 00:13:12.792
5100? Could you mean...?

00:13:16.458 --> 00:13:17.958
Too-too-roo!

00:13:17.958 --> 00:13:22.792
Guess what, Okarin! Mayushii
found out something amazing!

00:13:22.792 --> 00:13:28.208
--No cell phones.
--Faris-<i>chan </i>said she's seen the PC you're looking for!

00:13:28.208 --> 00:13:30.500
No cell phones!

00:13:35.167 --> 00:13:37.583
H-Hey!

00:13:37.583 --> 00:13:39.708
Geez...

00:13:39.708 --> 00:13:42.417
You didn't leave enough!

00:13:43.292 --> 00:13:51.833
Faris Meow-Meow! Faris Meow-Meow!
Faris Meow-Meow! Faris Meow-Meow!

00:13:51.833 --> 00:13:54.375
What is <i>this</i>?!

00:13:54.375 --> 00:13:56.083
Everyone!

00:13:56.083 --> 00:13:57.417
Thanks for coming, meow!

00:13:57.417 --> 00:14:00.042
We're about to start the daytime Faris Cup!

00:14:00.042 --> 00:14:02.125
Try your hardest to beat Faris

00:14:02.125 --> 00:14:06.167
and win an order of special
Meow-Meow Omelet Rice!

00:14:09.250 --> 00:14:12.500
Faris Meow-Meow! Faris Meow-Meow!

00:14:12.500 --> 00:14:15.542
Wh-What dimension <i>is </i>this?

00:14:15.542 --> 00:14:17.125
Oh, Okarin!

00:14:17.125 --> 00:14:18.958
Too-too-roo!

00:14:18.958 --> 00:14:20.583
Mayuri...

00:14:20.583 --> 00:14:23.667
What's going on here?
Was there a space-time distortion?!

00:14:23.667 --> 00:14:25.708
No, it's the Faris Cup!

00:14:25.708 --> 00:14:26.708
Huh?

00:14:26.708 --> 00:14:30.750
Faris-<i>chan </i>is going to play
Rai-Net Battler with all the visitors here!

00:14:30.750 --> 00:14:33.000
Oh, Kyouma!

00:14:33.000 --> 00:14:34.958
Are you going to compete too?

00:14:34.958 --> 00:14:37.917
Faris can play against
up to ten people at a time!

00:14:37.917 --> 00:14:40.125
--So it's not too late--
--I refuse!

00:14:40.125 --> 00:14:43.625
Never mind that! The IBN 5100! Where is it?!

00:14:43.625 --> 00:14:45.625
Well...

00:14:45.625 --> 00:14:48.917
I'll tell you if you compete.

00:14:48.917 --> 00:14:50.208
Don't be stupid!

00:14:50.208 --> 00:14:53.792
The future of the world's
structure hangs in the balance!

00:14:53.792 --> 00:14:58.292
--A silly game isn't--
--I'm sorry, then. Please leave.

00:14:58.292 --> 00:15:01.500
A lowly maid is telling her master to leave?!

00:15:01.500 --> 00:15:04.583
--The IBN 5100--
--Can't hear you!

00:15:06.250 --> 00:15:07.625
I'm in a hurry.

00:15:07.625 --> 00:15:10.750
I'm sorry, but I won't hold anything back.

00:15:10.750 --> 00:15:13.375
Meow, meow. You're really
confident in yourself, meow.

00:15:13.375 --> 00:15:14.792
Can you win, Okarin?

00:15:14.792 --> 00:15:17.208
Faris-<i>tan </i>is a top national player, you know...

00:15:17.208 --> 00:15:19.292
"Can you win?"

00:15:19.292 --> 00:15:22.125
You should ask <i>Faris </i>that question.

00:15:22.125 --> 00:15:25.083
I have a surefire,
infallible strategy up my sleeve!

00:15:25.083 --> 00:15:26.708
A strategy?

00:15:27.333 --> 00:15:29.167
Strategy Code...

00:15:29.167 --> 00:15:33.417
K.B.O.O.M.!

00:15:33.417 --> 00:15:36.042
Otherwise known as K-Boom!

00:15:36.042 --> 00:15:37.667
Oh!

00:15:37.667 --> 00:15:39.500
That sounds awesome!

00:15:39.500 --> 00:15:41.083
Interesting.

00:15:41.083 --> 00:15:44.083
Act tough now, while you still can.

00:15:44.083 --> 00:15:50.750
For when this strategy detonates,
you may very well lose your life!

00:15:50.750 --> 00:15:52.833
You're serious about this, Kyouma.

00:15:52.833 --> 00:15:54.375
Just so we're clear...

00:15:54.375 --> 00:15:59.333
Once I've participated,
you'll tell me everything you know.

00:15:59.333 --> 00:16:00.500
All right?

00:16:00.500 --> 00:16:02.917
Cat ears never lie.

00:16:02.917 --> 00:16:03.917
I challenge you!

00:16:03.917 --> 00:16:07.667
Now you'll learn there are some
opponents you can never beat!

00:16:07.667 --> 00:16:08.958
--I surrender!
--That was fast!

00:16:08.958 --> 00:16:11.542
Mayushii is disappointed.

00:16:11.542 --> 00:16:13.583
What the hell strategy was that?

00:16:13.583 --> 00:16:14.667
I'm not sure.

00:16:14.667 --> 00:16:19.083
But Kyouma kept charging at me,
like he <i>wanted </i>to go kaboom.

00:16:19.083 --> 00:16:20.250
Kaboom?

00:16:20.250 --> 00:16:21.792
K-Boom...

00:16:21.792 --> 00:16:23.292
K-Boom?

00:16:23.292 --> 00:16:25.875
Thank you very much
for that terrible word play.

00:16:25.875 --> 00:16:27.083
--However!
--WTF?!

00:16:27.083 --> 00:16:29.583
--Now tell me what you know, Faris!
--He recovers fast!

00:16:29.583 --> 00:16:32.417
You're stuck-up for someone who lost.

00:16:32.417 --> 00:16:36.583
I told you I'd participate only
if you told me what you know.

00:16:36.583 --> 00:16:40.125
In other words, winning never
mattered to me from the start.

00:16:40.125 --> 00:16:41.417
Is that right?

00:16:41.417 --> 00:16:42.917
I don't really remember...

00:16:42.917 --> 00:16:45.917
Remember it! It was an ingenious strategy!

00:16:45.917 --> 00:16:48.583
Ingenious? More like underhanded, I'd say...

00:16:48.583 --> 00:16:49.667
Shut up!

00:16:49.667 --> 00:16:51.875
Where's the IBN 5100?!

00:16:51.875 --> 00:16:54.417
--I don't know...
--You don't?!

00:16:54.417 --> 00:17:00.583
I know Daddy had one when
I was little, but it's gone now.

00:17:00.583 --> 00:17:01.833
Curses!

00:17:01.833 --> 00:17:04.583
Is that the secret sidestepping
technique you mastered

00:17:04.583 --> 00:17:06.375
in the Guiana Highlands?!

00:17:06.375 --> 00:17:08.542
How did you know?!

00:17:08.542 --> 00:17:14.208
Well done, Kyouma. You saw
right through my Ignoring Shoulder.

00:17:17.083 --> 00:17:18.583
Is that really all?

00:17:18.583 --> 00:17:24.333
Yeah. The last time I saw it
was at a shrine in Akihabara.

00:17:24.333 --> 00:17:26.083
A shrine?

00:17:26.083 --> 00:17:29.583
"Kurisu. Thank you for messaging
me all the way from Japan."

00:17:29.583 --> 00:17:33.500
"Regarding your query,
I consulted the professor and he said

00:17:33.500 --> 00:17:40.875
that the IBN 5100 could indeed
analyze special programming languages."

00:17:40.875 --> 00:17:42.708
He was telling the truth?

00:17:48.125 --> 00:17:50.250
Huh? A PC?

00:17:50.250 --> 00:17:52.708
I'd have to ask my father...

00:17:52.708 --> 00:17:54.667
It's an IBN 5100.

00:17:54.667 --> 00:17:57.583
If he doesn't recognize the name,
just say it's an old computer.

00:17:57.583 --> 00:17:59.875
Okay, I'll ask him.

00:17:59.875 --> 00:18:00.750
I'm counting on you.

00:18:00.750 --> 00:18:02.417
Now end with the code phrase...

00:18:02.417 --> 00:18:05.500
E-El Psy Congree...?

00:18:05.500 --> 00:18:07.125
Congroo!

00:18:10.167 --> 00:18:11.333
Hello?

00:18:11.333 --> 00:18:12.667
It's me, Makise.

00:18:12.667 --> 00:18:14.083
Makise?

00:18:14.083 --> 00:18:16.833
Sorry, doesn't ring a bell. Where did we meet?

00:18:16.833 --> 00:18:18.375
Paris? London?

00:18:18.375 --> 00:18:20.958
Akihabara. I just saw you!

00:18:20.958 --> 00:18:23.875
Oh, is that you, Assistant?

00:18:23.875 --> 00:18:25.792
You should've just said it's Christina.

00:18:25.792 --> 00:18:27.083
Don't call me that!

00:18:27.083 --> 00:18:29.250
Man, you're as loud and annoying as ever.

00:18:29.250 --> 00:18:31.417
Only because of a certain someone else!

00:18:31.417 --> 00:18:33.542
What do you want?

00:18:33.542 --> 00:18:34.750
Where are you?

00:18:34.750 --> 00:18:35.750
Why?

00:18:35.750 --> 00:18:37.375
No reason.

00:18:37.375 --> 00:18:40.917
I'm just on my way to Yanabayashi Shrine to--

00:18:42.125 --> 00:18:46.333
What?! Was that just a prank call?! Was it?!

00:18:46.333 --> 00:18:48.167
What was with that phone call?

00:18:48.167 --> 00:18:50.292
All I wanted was your location.

00:18:50.292 --> 00:18:52.583
I don't remember anyone asking you here.

00:18:52.583 --> 00:18:55.250
No one did.

00:18:56.167 --> 00:18:58.000
Sorry to keep you waiting!

00:18:58.000 --> 00:18:59.500
Oh, did you ask him?!

00:18:59.500 --> 00:19:05.125
Yes! My father said
there's one of those PCs here!

00:19:05.125 --> 00:19:07.875
--Really?!
--A PC...?

00:19:07.875 --> 00:19:10.250
Do you mean an IBN 5100?!

00:19:10.250 --> 00:19:11.292
Yes.

00:19:11.292 --> 00:19:14.042
--Umm, who might she be?
--My assistant.

00:19:14.042 --> 00:19:16.250
--So, the IBN--
--Hold on!

00:19:16.250 --> 00:19:19.167
What kind of offhand introduction is that?!

00:19:19.167 --> 00:19:21.292
Besides, I'm <i>not </i>your assistant!

00:19:21.292 --> 00:19:24.750
I didn't come here to introduce you!

00:19:24.750 --> 00:19:27.083
It wouldn't even take ten seconds!

00:19:27.083 --> 00:19:29.500
Geez, you're annoying.

00:19:29.500 --> 00:19:31.375
This is Makise Kurisu. My assistant.

00:19:31.375 --> 00:19:34.333
Fine, whatever. I'm your assistant.

00:19:34.333 --> 00:19:35.583
So who are you?

00:19:35.583 --> 00:19:37.875
I-I'm Urushibara Ruka.

00:19:37.875 --> 00:19:39.250
How old are you?

00:19:39.250 --> 00:19:42.542
--I turn seventeen this year.
--That's one year younger than me...

00:19:42.542 --> 00:19:44.958
Oh, really?

00:19:44.958 --> 00:19:47.417
You look so grown-up and mature, Makise-<i>san</i>.

00:19:47.417 --> 00:19:48.333
And pretty.

00:19:48.333 --> 00:19:50.792
Oh, no. You're much prettier.

00:19:50.792 --> 00:19:55.875
Huh? U-Umm... I'll go get my father!

00:19:55.875 --> 00:19:57.750
Ignorance is bliss, as they say.

00:19:57.750 --> 00:19:59.542
What do you mean?

00:20:00.667 --> 00:20:04.708
Wow, I can't believe it really happened...

00:20:04.708 --> 00:20:06.792
Wh-What do you mean?

00:20:06.792 --> 00:20:11.042
Well, you see, the person who
donated this computer also said

00:20:11.042 --> 00:20:17.500
to take good care of it, for a young
man in need of it would someday appear.

00:20:17.500 --> 00:20:20.375
About ten years ago, I'd say?

00:20:20.375 --> 00:20:22.917
I see.

00:20:22.917 --> 00:20:25.000
This is truly a coincidence of fate...

00:20:25.000 --> 00:20:26.750
The choice of Steins Gate!

00:20:26.750 --> 00:20:28.792
Not that again...

00:20:34.958 --> 00:20:38.417
IBN 5100 Portable Computer.

00:20:38.417 --> 00:20:39.875
No doubt about it.

00:20:39.875 --> 00:20:42.208
Is that what you're looking for?

00:20:42.208 --> 00:20:44.417
Umm, could we possibly borrow it?!

00:20:44.417 --> 00:20:46.667
Of course.

00:20:46.667 --> 00:20:48.208
Thank you!

00:20:48.208 --> 00:20:50.125
--Assistant! Haul this back!
--No u.

00:20:50.125 --> 00:20:51.875
What kind of assistant are you, Christina?!

00:20:51.875 --> 00:20:54.875
I'm <i>not </i>your assistant! And don't call me that!

00:20:54.875 --> 00:20:57.667
I'll go get a cart.

00:20:57.667 --> 00:21:00.542
Oh, no, we couldn't ask any more of you!

00:21:00.542 --> 00:21:03.458
Hey, Assistant! Take a hint, will you?!

00:21:03.458 --> 00:21:08.500
Huh?! <i>You're </i>telling <i>me </i>to talk a hint?!

00:21:08.500 --> 00:21:10.625
You're certainly good friends, I see.

00:21:10.625 --> 00:21:13.333
Be a good friend to them too, Ruka.

00:21:13.333 --> 00:21:15.417
Right!

00:21:15.417 --> 00:21:18.125
Wait here a moment.

00:21:20.125 --> 00:21:21.917
You have a nice father.

00:21:21.917 --> 00:21:24.042
Do you think so?

00:21:24.042 --> 00:21:27.542
I won't repeat my father's failure!

00:21:29.542 --> 00:21:30.500
What?

00:21:30.500 --> 00:21:32.667
Nothing.

00:21:32.667 --> 00:21:34.208
I'm sorry!

00:21:34.208 --> 00:21:37.417
The cart seems to be broken...

00:21:40.167 --> 00:21:42.667
How did I get stuck doing this with you?!

00:21:42.667 --> 00:21:46.292
Just shut up and carry it.
We've still a long way to go!

00:21:50.250 --> 00:21:52.042
--Say...
--What?

00:21:52.042 --> 00:21:53.833
Never mind!

00:21:53.833 --> 00:21:57.750
What's with the attitude, you?!

00:21:57.750 --> 00:22:00.500
Hey! Wait! You're making me walk backwards!

00:22:00.500 --> 00:22:03.625
Walk briskly, Assistant!

00:22:03.625 --> 00:22:06.167
I can't! I can't do this walking backwards!

00:22:06.167 --> 00:22:07.875
I know you can do it, Assistant!

00:22:07.875 --> 00:22:10.458
Thank you for the encouragement! But I can't!

00:22:10.458 --> 00:22:12.333
I request we walk sideways!

00:22:12.333 --> 00:22:15.958
No, we<i> have </i>to! Or I'm gonna fall!

00:22:27.208 --> 00:22:35.167
<i>kisei sareta shikai mujihi naru</i>

00:22:36.167 --> 00:22:43.917
<i>juuni no shihai nogarerarenai</i>

00:22:43.917 --> 00:22:52.792
<i>ansoku no asu o negatta</i>

00:22:52.792 --> 00:23:01.500
<i>te no naka no toutoi jishou no chihei e</i>

00:23:01.500 --> 00:23:10.125
<i>torawareshi meiyaku</i>
<i>arawareta gishou no rinkaku</i>

00:23:10.125 --> 00:23:19.250
<i>seimei no tenchi wa</i>
<i>moumoku na jikan o kizanda</i>

00:23:19.250 --> 00:23:28.125
<i>habatake batafurai kiseki</i>
<i>no batafurai anata e sasagu</i>

00:23:28.125 --> 00:23:35.292
<i>namida no batafurai</i>
<i>mabushii batafurai subete ga</i>

00:23:35.292 --> 00:24:02.027
<i>ima kakikaerareru</i>
